1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.370
[S01] It kind of happened unexpectedly because I so I came to LA and I was like, okay, I gotta find a place to live.

2
00:00:05.849 --> 00:00:12.539
[S01] And I had no money because I also had credit card debt because I was like working for free and it was just, you know, the whole thing moving out.

3
00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:17.940
[S01] And so I got a job working at a restaurant in in West Hollywood.

4
00:00:18.239 --> 00:00:23.820
[S01] It was like a lot of people from the film business came to this restaurant and I became friendly with this couple.

5
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.350
[S01] And we would talk design and go to museums and I would tell them I was going to the flea market and.

6
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:34.829
[S01] And they were like, hey, why not like, do you want to help us with our house? We just got a house in Venice in the canals.

7
00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:41.969
[S01] And we, you know, we'll give you like the living room and like you work on that and like there was no budget.

8
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.460
[S01] So I'm like, yes, like I'm gonna do this. And I was doing everything like I was painting.

9
00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:54.450
[S01] I was going to the the paint store in the morning, finding the painter, painting, going to the flea market with a flashlight in the morning.

10
00:00:54.659 --> 00:01:01.170
[S01] At like five in the morning, we find all the like good stuff and like like having a cart, putting things in my car.

11
00:01:01.679 --> 00:01:07.019
[S01] I was doing everything because I wanted this project so bad to to just be amazing.

12
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.549
[S02] Did you think about it as like a formative project or were you just doing your mates a favor?

13
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:17.250
[S02] Like, was there a point in your mind where you're like, oh, this is gonna be like a some kind of showroom for me or like, you know?

14
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.920
[S01] No, I wasn't. I was just doing what I felt in my heart. Like, I wanted to make the clients happy.

15
00:01:23.099 --> 00:01:28.019
[S01] It was kind of like the perfect storm. So I did the one room and then I ended up doing the entire house.

16
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:33.510
[S01] And then, you know, they had friends over and I ended up getting other projects.

17
00:01:33.629 --> 00:01:39.510
[S01] And so I was like, like shit, I have my my own business. But I was still working out of my apartment.

18
00:01:39.519 --> 00:01:46.980
[S01] I was doing, I was still waiting tables like I, because you're nervous. It's like, what is the next job I'm gonna get? Like, I didn't know.

19
00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:54.420
[S01] And so then I started getting a couple of calls and then I was like, this is amazing. And I ended up hiring.

20
00:01:54.659 --> 00:02:01.019
[S01] Um, an assistant who actually worked at a vintage store that was like so great and and he was helping me in my apartment.

21
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:08.669
[S02] So this really was like born out of a passion and you just like throwing yourself in and then word of mouth.

22
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:09.599
[S01] Yes.

23
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:10.050
[S02] That was it.

24
00:02:10.379 --> 00:02:13.379
[S01] There was no Instagram. There was no like advertising.

25
00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:19.409
[S02] So there's no way of publicizing your work. It's like if you got invited to that couple's house and was like, oh, this is like a lovely living room.

26
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:23.129
[S02] Or a lovely home, they would say, oh, Kelly did this.

27
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:28.139
[S02] Was it a scary decision? Because again, I speak to so many young founders.

28
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:35.729
[S02] And I think that people that are sitting here and listening to this at home that are dreaming of like jumping into something that they really love.

29
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:41.789
[S02] But it's not quite like the thing that they dream about is not quite matching their, you know, day job, if you like.

30
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.870
[S02] Was there trepidation from you, like giving up waiting tables or like?

31
00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:47.009
[S01] Yes, oh my god, I would have.
